<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!--
  gLRC repair experiment configuration (two orthogonal axes; classic C0-C3 pairs).

  [Axis 1] Execution architecture — GlrcRepairMode (how repair runs / who executes)
    phase1   One anchor repair proxy pulls all helpers, decodes full blocks, writes back.
             Good for f=1 or as a baseline; all helper traffic goes through the anchor proxy.
    phase2   Shard by GlrcShardCount; each failed-block partition runs on its own datanode
             repair proxy in parallel (partial read + shard decode + proxy exchange).
             For f>1 each partition uses bandwidth independently.
    pipeline Shard by GlrcShardCount; multiple equation chains run in parallel; GlrcPipelineWindow
             controls in-flight shards (true pipeline). Hub is the survivor proxy in the most
             equations; a local single failure may use local-direct and skip the Hub.

  [Axis 2] Equation selection — GlrcEquationPolicy (which repair equations to use)
    local-then-global  Ceph-style: prefer local XOR, then global Cauchy equations.
    local-first        Recommended for pipeline: prefer local equation sets, then add global.
    ilp-min-helper     ILP search: among solvable plans, minimize the helper-block union.

  Typical combinations (change the two tags below; no code changes needed):
    C0: phase1 + local-then-global   (default Phase1 baseline)
    C1: phase2 + local-then-global
    C2: phase1 + ilp-min-helper
    C3: phase2 + ilp-min-helper

  Other gLRC knobs:
    GlrcShardCount         Number of shards; BlockSize must be divisible by it.
    GlrcPipelineWindow     In-flight shard window W on a pipeline chain;
                           0 = W=GlrcShardCount (full pipeline); 1 = serial W=1.
    GlrcPhase2WriteBack    Whether phase2 writes repaired blocks back to datanodes
                           (set false for repeated random trials if desired).
    NodeBlockBandwidthMBps Per-node NIC unidirectional bandwidth (MB/s); 0 = unlimited.
                           Stable model: hop->hop rate-limits sender egress; hub/sink
                           aggregation rate-limits receiver ingress (no egress limit toward
                           the aggregation point, to avoid dual-sided sleep deadlocking TCP).
                           Same-host DN<->proxy is unlimited; cross-host DN->proxy uses DN.egress.
                           Note: waiting on both ends of one TCP connection in software often
                           stalls, so intermediate hops do not also rate-limit RX.

  Preconditions: CodeType must be gLRC; ClusterNum >= z.
-->
<Configuration>
    <AlignedSize>4096</AlignedSize>
    <UnitSize>8192</UnitSize>
    <BlockSize>67108864</BlockSize>

    <!-- Per-node unidirectional bandwidth: 125 MB/s (1 Gbps); ingress/egress independent -->
    <NodeBlockBandwidthMBps>125</NodeBlockBandwidthMBps>

    <!-- Repair mode: phase1 | phase2 | pipeline | hybrid -->
    <GlrcRepairMode>hybrid</GlrcRepairMode>
    <GlrcHybridP>auto</GlrcHybridP>
    <!-- Equation policy: local-then-global | local-first | ilp-min-helper -->
    <GlrcEquationPolicy>local-then-global</GlrcEquationPolicy>

    <GlrcShardCount>128</GlrcShardCount>
    <GlrcPipelineWindow>0</GlrcPipelineWindow>
    <GlrcPhase2WriteBack>true</GlrcPhase2WriteBack>

    <!-- Real-system: z=4 gLRC placement groups over 55 storage nodes. -->
    <DatanodeNumPerCluster>14</DatanodeNumPerCluster>
    <ClusterNum>4</ClusterNum>
    <CoordinatorIP>172.16.3.68</CoordinatorIP>
    <CoordinatorPort>55555</CoordinatorPort>
    <ClientIP>172.16.3.75</ClientIP>
    <ClientPort>55555</ClientPort>

    <AppendMode>UNILRC_MODE</AppendMode>
    <alpha>2</alpha>

    <CodeType>gLRC</CodeType>
    <!-- n=55: k=48 data, r=3 global parity G, z=4 local parity L; k+r split evenly across z groups -->
    <k>48</k>
    <r>3</r>
    <z>4</z>

</Configuration>
